   "text": {
    "L1": "Infrastructure is the basic set of facilities and systems a country needs to function.",
    "L2": "It is an engine of development because it connects people, services, supplies and markets.",
    "L3": "For example, an all-weather road lets farmers take produce to town and get better prices.",
    "L4": "The same road helps children reach school and patients reach hospitals in time.",
    "L5": "Infrastructure is physical, social and digital: roads and power, schools and hospitals, and mobile or internet networks.",
    "L6": "But building it can take land and affect forests or rivers, so planning must be fair and careful.",
    "L7": "Infrastructure also needs regular maintenance and should be sustainable, such as solar power or metro rail.",
    "L8": "Now check the idea: which example is social infrastructure?"
   },
